WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.770
In 2024, India's biggest
customer for goods was the USA:

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.510
18.3 per cent of its goods exports.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.110
Its biggest supplier was China:
18.2 per cent of its goods imports.

4
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.150
Trade made up 45.9 per cent
of India's GDP in 2024,

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.970
up from 15.5 per cent in 1990.

6
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.330
So what does two-way trade do to
a fast-growing country like India?

7
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.310
In this mission, you'll
map what India sells,

8
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.350
who it trades with, and
how that has changed.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.250
Then you'll judge trade's
impacts on development,

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.930
equality and stability,
with a figure for each.

11
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: assess what
two-way trade does to India,

12
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.930
a fast-growing country.
